 In Rust, you can use match statements instead of multiple if-else conditions for this task. Here's the equivalent code in Rust:

```rust
fn is_even(n: i32) -> bool {
 match n {
     0 => true,
     1 | 3 | 5 | 7 | 9 => false,
     _ => {
         if n % 2 == 0 {
             true
         } else {
