This version of the function `is_even` checks if the number is even using a match statement with exhaustive patterns. The first few cases cover the numbers from 0 through 9 that we checked in the JavaScript example. For all other numbers, it uses the modulo operator `%` to check if the remainder when dividing by 2 is zero, which indicates an even number.

